# scaleup_single_switch_4_3600Gbps.topo
#
# Models an NVLink-class SCALE-UP domain as a single non-blocking crossbar:
# 4 hosts (GPUs) all attached to ONE ToR switch, every pair exactly one hop apart.
# Per-host link = 3600 Gbps (NVLink-aggregate class); switch latency 300 ns, link 500 ns.
#
# Degenerate 2-tier encoding (Tiers=1 is rejected by the FatTree parser): Podsize ==
# Nodes and Tier-0 Radix_Down == Nodes => one ToR holds all hosts; Radix_Up 1 vestigial;
# Oversubscribed == Nodes keeps radix_down/radix_up == oversub. Sibling of the _16 topo,
# scaled to 4 hosts for the INC-vs-ring speedup-vs-N sweep (D3, radix == |G|).
Nodes 4
Tiers 2
Podsize 4

Tier 0
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 4
Radix_Up 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 300
Oversubscribed 4

Tier 1
Downlink_speed_Gbps 3600
Radix_Down 1
Downlink_Latency_ns 500
Switch_Latency_ns 300
